Ticket #4471 does not contain one problem. Tenant locale, booking-form version, report
channel, and the desk's follow-up separate its reports into three causes.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Engineering tickets

- [Shared parser flips day-first dates](https://github.com/rozmarin-2013/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)
  — **fixed**. The desk moved five one-day-move reports to separate work, so this ticket covers
  374 reports.
- [booking-v3 shows the wrong date-order hint](https://github.com/rozmarin-2013/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)
  — **won't fix**. The affected form is retired; this ticket covers 33 reports.
- [One-day date moves require separate investigation](https://github.com/rozmarin-2013/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3)
  — **open**. The desk moved these 5 reports out of the parser work after review.

<Callout>
Desk update, 5 October: #4471 is closed. The parser fix shipped; the booking-v3 hint will not
be changed because the form is retired.
</Callout>

## Shared parser

The shared parser reads dates month-first. For tenants whose locale writes the day first,
dates with two valid month numbers are silently flipped. This affects app, email, and form
reports. It covers 374 reports after the desk moved five reports to separate work.

## booking-v3 hint

`booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. Day-first tenants follow that hint, but
the form reads the entered value in the tenant's order. This is a separate form problem, even
when the report subject matches a parser report.

## One-day moves

Five reports do not describe a day/month swap. They describe a one-day or weekday shift, an
invite before its booking, or the same meeting landing on different weekdays. The desk moved
them to separate work after the first review, so they need their own open ticket.

<Callout>
The subject line and intake tag are not enough to deduplicate these reports. Classify them by
tenant locale, booking-form version, and channel.
</Callout>

## Triage change

Keep one engineering ticket per cause. Deduplicate overlapping export rows by report ID before
counting. A desk move is stronger evidence than the intake tag, so move those reports out of
the parser group when the desk reclassifies them.

